WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.035 size:75% position:38%
-Holidays coming up.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will you spend Thanksgiving
with your family?

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.405
-Yes. We celebrate. We go
to the beach in North Carolina.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
My brother David
bought us a house,

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:09.242
which we call "The Sea Section."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we do a -- we do a
Mediterranean Thanksgiving,

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause my dad´s 94,
and we´re Greek.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so now we just make
a big Greek --

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:18.885
-And any family traditions,
other than the Mediterranean?

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. [ Laughs ]

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
I turn the living room
into spa night,

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I give everybody a facial.
-[ Laughing ] Okay.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I hire my sister in-law,
who does all the work,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I´m very abusive to her.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s just for "entertainment."
-Yeah.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:30.930 size:78% position:39%
-And I never give her
a cut of the money.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then my niece helps me
with the invitations.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everyone just complains.
-Oh, that´s wonderful.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what I mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.471
-But then, they´re sound asleep
by the end of the night,

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I really don´t know
what I´m doing.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.207 size:81% position:41%
But, I mean, you know,

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have good skin in my family.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No one ever moisturizes,
you know?

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-So...

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. They want --
They want that tape nose skin.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they want
the tape nose skin.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.516
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-So I love doing it. It´s great.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you have any tips
on entertaining

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:53.920
during the holidays -- do you --
when you have people over?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I always say, you know,
just be prepared.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
there will be some accidents.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
But just take
a Polaroid picture of it

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.928
and laugh at it in a few years.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I always hate it
when you go to someone´s house

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they invite you
for Thanksgiving

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you walk in

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the raw Turkey
is sitting out on the counter.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.503
You´re like, "Damn it. I don´t
want to be here for five hours!"

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Right.
-That´s not fair.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it´s not. No.
-That is not fair.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you´re -- they
just encourage you to drink,

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.511
and then they have cheese balls
and snacks,

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.346 size:88% position:44%
and then you´re stuffed.
-That´s the problem --

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
my biggest --
and I hold myself accountable.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.018
The amount of, like, early dairy
you eat on Thanksgiving.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of early dairy.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:27.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, you know, it´s like...
-Yes.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.122
-..."Oh, dinner´s gonna be ready
in two -- two hours."

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.457
And you´re like, "Well, then,
I´ll eat a pound of cheese,

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.524
and then I´ll be very happy."

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I´ll be in a great mood
later on."

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.563 size:88% position:44%
-Yes, you´re so right.
It is a pound of cheese.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.531
-You -- I hear that you --

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
you keep things in your fridge
that are not food

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you then gift?

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.671
-Oh, I like to have some artwork
in my refrigerator.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.739
-Okay, so why -- why -- why?

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.109
-Because, "A," it´s always nice
when you open your refrigerator

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.443
and you see that cut-off hand --

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.644 size:81% position:41%
you know, you get them
at Halloween stores.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.912
It´s just a hand that´s cut off,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they --
they wrap it really nice.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.783
It´s like from Chop Shop or
something -- that name´s bad.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.984
But it´s in nice Saran Wrap.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.119
And then I have a nice --

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So that´s just a thing
that you have

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.755
that you want other people
to see, or you take joy?

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:06.292
-Well, I showed it to my godson,
and I saw the look on his face,

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I just --
just changed the subject.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was --
Yeah, that was not cool.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, yeah.
-That wasn´t -- yeah.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that´s not something
he can unsee.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.367
-No, I moved it to the freezer.
It´s cool.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, but it is nice

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you open it up,
and you can see artwork.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.472
I have a nice fake milk carton.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have some fake butter boxes
that I made.

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.712
-And it doesn´t -- it doesn´t
take up valuable fridge space?

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Oh, that´s good.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just have lettuce in there
for Tina, really.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, great.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I don´t know
how to tell you this,

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on her carpet...
-Thanks.

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.554 size:78% position:39%
-...but I don´t know
if she loves lettuce.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.390
-I know, really high piles.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.859
-So you -- you´ve been on
a lot of television shows.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the first time
you are running your own show.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I have -- Do you love it?

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.432
-I liked it, but it was like --

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.101
you know, well, first thing,
doing all those characters,

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.435
I realized, "Wow," you know.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn´t realize
I had to memorize

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
both sides of the script.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what I mean?
So that was like --

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.908
- Right, ´cause you interact
with the characters themselves.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Then I´m like,
"Oh, what was I thinking?"

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you know
what I learned most?

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m not kidding --
it´s this e-mail etiquette...

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.147
-Okay.
-...you know, that people have.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just learned how to
"reply all."

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or, you know,
whose name goes first.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
And people pay attention
to that stuff.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.656
It never even entered my mind to
think about that kind of stuff.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:12.692
-What -- Like, how -- What do
you mean about "reply all"?

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
You never had any reason
until you had your own show?

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just reply.
I don´t reply all.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.930
And then,
I hate it when people reply all,

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you open your e-mail,
it´s like, "K,"

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, "Thanks. Awesome."
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, don´t bother me.
-Yeah.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My mom´s motto was,
"Don´t bother other people."

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In general?
-I think that´s a good --

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.707
Yeah, don´t bother other people.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that -- Was that something
when you were kids?

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How excited you are,
like there´s something deep.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, no. No, I don´t mean
there´s something deep,

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, like, as kids,

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.051
were you under instructions
not to be a bother to people?

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, no.
We -- My mom --

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, you just
don´t bother other --

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
We could bother each other,
I guess,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.023
and we could bother our parents.
We just don´t bother.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.525
You know, like,
when someone comes to your house

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they say,
"Do you have any scissors?"

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s like, "You know I do."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.330
I have a craft book out.
Just ask me where they are.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don´t ask me
if I have them there.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just puts me in a bad mood.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I want to stab them
with it, you know?

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.037 size:88% position:44%
Well, I have another one
that I can tell you...

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
-...is when people say,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Can I ask you a question?"
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-´Cause that´s
already a question.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes, right.
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.645
-So they´ve already taken the
leap of asking me a question.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or else they
wouldn´t have said it.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.983
-And then you ask it, and then
they say, "No, you cannot ask."

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.184
And you´re just, "All right.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.019
That´s some Whitney Houston..."
you know.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she does that
in the documentary.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, she does?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that´s great.
-It´s a great documentary.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Whitney Houston
documentary?

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it´s fun.
-Is it recent?

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:19.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it´s recent.
-Okay.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the George Michael one.
I´m in documentary mode.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.595
-The George Michael one,
I´ve heard, is fantastic.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it really is.
-Yeah.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.265
-I think they leave some stuff
out, but I guess you have to.

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:26.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I like it because
it´s about a singer, you know?

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re just out there,
by themselves, performing.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s interesting. But
I guess you do it every night.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:32.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not like George Michael
or Whitney Houston.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Come on. Come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, just on a talent level,
like, that´s the thing.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.244
People who said they watched
the George Michael documentary

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.280
were overwhelmed by how --
exactly how talented he was.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and how ambitious.
-Yeah.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:44.183
-Like when you´re little, be
like, "I want to be a big star."

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I guess I wouldn´t --

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:46.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
I´d be less interested

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
in watching a documentary
about comedians.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right, right.
-Because then I would --

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.024
anybody who said, like --

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
Any time I would see somebody
working really hard,

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´d be like,
"Oh, I should work harder."

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] I know, right?
-Whereas, like, when I --

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.230
when you watch Whitney Houston
or George Michael and be like,

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.464
"Oh, I never had that voice."

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would never, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wow, what a voice.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What a voice.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Also, he´s somebody who
I did not quite understand --

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
when he sadly passed away,

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.707
I had no sense of
what a wonderful person he was.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, same here.

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like
I´d missed all that,

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:11.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I felt really bad,
but also, you know,

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
very impressed
with the kind of guy he was.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.480
-Right. Plus,
he passed away on Christmas Day.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn´t realize that.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
Christmas Day.
-Well --

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess last year.
-Yeah.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.252 size:75% position:38%
-But you´re gonna --

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.386
Your parents are coming in town
for Thanksgiving?

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My parents
are gonna come to town.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re gonna be on this show
on Thursday.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, and then
will you go to New Hampshire

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.425 size:78% position:39%
to have Thanksgiving?

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, they´re gonna stay here
in the city.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, will you go to a
restaurant, or you gonna cook?

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, we´re gonna have them
at our apartment.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, and you´re gonna cook,
or did you --

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
